Applying machine learning to sensor data is one of the most valuable uses of ML today — from predictive maintenance and anomaly detection to human activity recognition and robotics.

-cOLLECT DATA sENSORS:
Time-series from one or more sensors
Sensors like accelerometers, gyroscopes, temperature, etc.
Data coming in real-time or stored in logs (CSV, JSON, etc.)

-Preprocess / Clean the Data
Handle missing values (NaN, 0, gaps)
Resample (uniform time intervals)
Denoise (moving average, Savitzky-Golay, or Kalman filter)
Normalize or standardize values (scale features)

-Feature Engineering
Extract meaningful information from raw signals. Common techniques:

🧠 Time-Domain Features
Mean, std dev, min, max, variance
Signal energy or zero-crossing rate
Rolling statistics (moving mean/std)

-Frequency-Domain Features (via FFT)
Dominant frequency
Spectral entropy
Energy in specific frequency bands

- Sensor Fusion Features
Combine multiple sensor channels (e.g., combine x/y/z of accelerometer)
Vector magnitude:

-Custom Domain Features
Heart rate from ECG
Angular velocity from gyroscope
Temperature rise rate

-. Labeling (if supervised learning)
You’ll need labels for:
Classification (e.g., "running", "walking", "falling")
Regression (e.g., estimate force, time-to-fail)
Labels can come from:
Manual annotations
Rules (e.g., thresholds)
Events (e.g., machine failure time)

-Modeling: Choose a Machine Learning Algorithm
| Goal              | ML Model                           |
| ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Classification    | RandomForest, SVM, Neural Networks |
| Regression        | LinearRegression, SVR, XGBoost     |
| Sequence modeling | RNN, LSTM, GRU                     |
| Anomaly detection | Isolation Forest, Autoencoder      |


-Training & Validation
Split into train/test (e.g. 80/20 or time-based)
Use k-fold if applicable
Evaluate with metrics:
Classification: Accuracy, F1, Confusion Matrix
Regression: MAE, MSE, R²

-Deploy / Monitor
Deploy model in real-time pipeline (e.g., on Raspberry Pi or server)
Monitor sensor input → apply preprocessing → predict


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Steps:
Preprocess (resample, normalize)

Feature extraction: Vector magnitude of accel,Rolling mean/std AND FFT peak
Train classifier (e.g., RandomForest)
Predict activity for new data

| Step                | What to Do                                |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Collect             | Get sensor streams                        |
| Preprocess          | Clean, resample, normalize                |
| Feature Engineering | Extract meaningful stats from raw signals |
| Modeling            | Choose classifier or regressor            |
| Evaluate            | Use metrics to validate model             |
| Deploy              | Real-time pipeline or batch prediction    |

